  "body": "PR2628 supplies a completed-instruction stability contract for PR2540's full QQ16 decoder. This adds a separately written, JSON-only reverse-covector audit of **all 2,680 initialized changed-field boundaries**, all five peak metrics and all **464 final-field envelopes**, without importing or executing predecessor code. It corroborates P=240, A=1529, K=2298, native=192 and cover=280, plus a separate literal execution of the existing 841-error transient.\n\nThe same feedback inequality permits **u <= 2^(-b-20)** for every integer b>=0: its exact uniform threshold is K(P+1)=553818 <= 2^20. PR2628's 21-bit allowance remains correct. Twenty is the smallest uniform integer guard furnished by this particular inequality; failure of its 19-bit majorant is not an impossibility result for another analysis or physical implementation.\n\nSources are pinned byte-exactly: PR2628 `e64a7babb285f22baeee89a9d88f5e79c512909a`, PR2540 `630d557af5088f66b45c447969cee9576600e50b`, and main's immutable QQ16 owner registry. New work starts from canonical main `b4560d9e7216f72b73c5aa940ac099c05e33ccf9`, priority revision 5. TASK records the sole task-selection draw, scope change, overlap and remaining obligation. [Canonical investigation](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2648).\n\nValidation:\n\n- CPython 3.12.14 registered replay: `python3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/qq16-defect-independent-audit`.\n- CPython 3.14.7 optimized primary and nine behavioral control groups.\n- Read-only, Git-free export: eleven files unchanged after primary and controls.\n- Controls cover retained capture errors, signed cancellation, noncommuting route order, escaped scratch errors, approximate borrowed restoration, chronology/uninitialized dirt, the feedback threshold and source corruption.\n\nThis audits coefficient propagation under the credited unitary/frame and exact-owned-CLEAR premises. Entry/F0/B1 bounds, child internals, physical component rounding, retention/movement/hosting and supplier admission remain open. No selected frontier, frozen source, decoder word or invoice changes; no new kappa, human review, proof-assistant, hosted-CI or selected cold-replay pass is claimed.\n\nCredit ywz65's PR2511/2512/2540/2603/2628, the PR2096/2166/2503 stability lineage, Ali Romman, thakrarsagar, starship-s, Ross Richardson and the retained geometry/native sources. New checker, controls and guard refinement by Arham Tahir with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance. Apache-2.0.\n",
